al evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also substantially complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state and boot identities were captured, restart acknowledgements were recorded, post-restart identities differ and match the fixed lifecycle observations, persistent configuration recovered, and both nodes returned to synchronized service. The only notable hygiene defect is an accidental second reboot of node1.","limitations":["Node1's Chrony client table uses an environment hostname rather than explicitly labeling the client as node2; however, node2 independently and directly reports node1's address as its contacted server with a completed packet exchange.","Node1 was rebooted twice. Evidence covers the intermediate changed identity, acknowledgement of the second reboot, final changed identity, and final recovery, but the extra transition was unnecessary."]}
